# Classic Cuts Skill maintenance

Canonical project Skill: `.agents/skills/classic-cuts-website/` (`SKILL.md` + `references/`).

That Skill stays **Classic Cuts–specific**. Do not move it into a global Skill.

Global reusable website extracts (if installed) live outside this repo:

```text
~/.cursor/skills/future-proof-designers/custom-business-websites/
```

Related global Skills (do not replace this project Skill):

```text
~/.cursor/skills/future-proof-designers/project-bootstrap/
~/.cursor/skills/future-proof-designers/production-saas-patterns/
```

`production-saas-patterns` applies only at the external booking/SaaS boundary — never as a mandate to rewrite this static marketing site.

## Before declaring a meaningful feature complete

Ask two independent questions:

**A. Did this change alter durable Classic Cuts website knowledge?**

If **yes** → update the **relevant** `classic-cuts-website` reference file(s) in the same feature commit when practical (and `SKILL.md` only if the index/invariants changed).

If **no** → leave the project Skill unchanged.

**B. Did we discover a genuinely reusable website lesson that would still apply if the next project were not Classic Cuts and not a barbershop?**

If **yes** → consider promoting a *generalized* principle into `custom-business-websites` (principle first; Classic Cuts only as a labeled origin example). Strip business names, addresses, phones, tenant IDs, deployment IDs, and exact brand tokens.

If **no** → do not touch global Skills.

Global promotion is **optional and uncommon**. A typo, spacing tweak, one image swap, temporary deploy, one QA result, or minor copy change is never a global update. A new booking-embed failure pattern or mobile CTA invariant might be.

Do **not** copy Classic Cuts references wholesale into the global Skill. Review the global diff before writing.

## Update when changing

- Page architecture or routing (`vercel.json` public paths)
- Design-system tokens / typography / button hierarchy
- Navigation / chrome behavior
- Hero / primary conversion path
- BookLocal (or other) embed integration boundary
- Performance strategy (LCP, fonts, video gates)
- SEO structure (canonical patterns, structured data approach)
- Accessibility invariants
- Deployment/caching architecture
- New failure mode worth documenting

## Do **not** update for

- One-off copy edits, single image swaps, minor spacing
- Temporary preview URLs or deploy IDs
- Ephemeral QA notes
- Uncommitted experiments

## Conflicts

If Skill documentation conflicts with **current website source**, inspect the source and **correct the Skill**.  
Do **not** modify correct production pages merely to satisfy stale docs.

## Style

- Prefer targeted edits over rewriting the whole Skill
- Never commit secrets, keys, or unnecessary PII into Skill files
- Skill updates must be visible in Git diff (no silent memory)
- Do not auto-rewrite the Skill from every chat turn
